        "body": "# Motif v0.5.0\n\nMotif v0.5.0 redesigns the workbench for calmer, more predictable sequence work and corrects a broad set of cloning, primer, and GenBank results.\n\nThis is the first published release since v0.3.6. It also includes the changes listed under 0.4.0 in the changelog, which were not published as a separate release.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- A redesigned workbench: the record's facts and actions sit on one top bar, records live in a Library pane, a labeled Tools drawer holds the tools, and controls share one height and text scale. Inventory is now Library, Add Entry is Import records, and Database JSON is Workspace JSON.\n- Light is the default theme, with a light/dark button in the top bar. The two warm themes are retired; a saved warm theme opens in Light or Dark.\n- A Find bar (Cmd/Ctrl+F), a right-click menu on the sequence, and edit notices with their own Undo. A click changes the selection and leaves the view where it is, and selecting a feature in the sequence or on the map selects it in both.\n- The circular map shows full feature names and lists unnamed features in its \"+N features\" tooltip. Translation opens in its own window, and translation rows follow the strand.\n- Corrected results across restriction cut positions, PCR primer sites that cross the origin, melting temperatures, Golden Gate and Gibson junctions, open reading frames, and Sanger read mapping. GenBank import and export keep more of a record.\n- Each pane recovers from its own error, the full enzyme list on a long record no longer crashes the workbench, and edits in large multi-record workspaces are much faster.\n- Release rollback now restores only the Motif connector entry and keeps the other servers in your configuration.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Saved construct verification reports can carry two new optional read fields, `cigar` and `searchIncomplete`. Earlier releases reject a report that has them, so keep a copy saved by your earlier release if you need to open it there.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 4,014 unit tests\n- 580 core browser workflow tests\n- 80 dedicated MSA interaction tests\n- Plugin manifest validation\n- Node 22 and Node 24 compatibility checks\n- CodeQL, dependency policy, reproducibility, release-budget, and supply-chain verification\n- Zero known npm audit vulnerabilities at publication\n\nThe supported installer verifies the release against the separately published manifest digest before changing connector configuration.\n",
